From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 02:29:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] spi: apple-qspi: runtime suspend the T8132 controller

The T8132 boot NOR controller probes without runtime PM, so its QSPI
power domain stays on for as long as the system runs. A read of the
PMGR power-state words on a J604 running Linux shows the domain fully
on at idle. macOS on the same machine programs the domain's target
state to off during early boot and leaves it there.

Use the runtime PM path that the T8140 controller already takes: a
100 ms autosuspend delay around spi-mem operations, the IRQ disabled
before genpd gates the block, and a controller reset on resume to
restore timing, FIFO thresholds and interrupt state. Reads stay single
I/O on T8132; only the power policy changes.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 drivers/spi/spi-apple-qspi.c | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/spi/spi-apple-qspi.c b/drivers/spi/spi-apple-qspi.c
index 06e2d356dc..cf11c31add 100644
--- a/drivers/spi/spi-apple-qspi.c
+++ b/drivers/spi/spi-apple-qspi.c
@@ -1264,6 +1264,10 @@ static const struct dev_pm_ops apple_qspi_pm_ops = {
 
 static const struct apple_qspi_soc apple_qspi_single_io = { };
 
+static const struct apple_qspi_soc apple_qspi_t8132 = {
+	.runtime_pm = true,
+};
+
 static const struct apple_qspi_soc apple_qspi_t8140 = {
 	.multi_io_reads = true,
 	.runtime_pm = true,
@@ -1271,7 +1275,7 @@ static const struct apple_qspi_soc apple_qspi_t8140 = {
 
 static const struct of_device_id apple_qspi_of_match[] = {
 	{ .compatible = "apple,t8122-qspi", .data = &apple_qspi_single_io },
-	{ .compatible = "apple,t8132-qspi", .data = &apple_qspi_single_io },
+	{ .compatible = "apple,t8132-qspi", .data = &apple_qspi_t8132 },
 	{ .compatible = "apple,t6041-qspi", .data = &apple_qspi_single_io },
 	{ .compatible = "apple,t8140-qspi", .data = &apple_qspi_t8140 },
 	{}
